  "notes": "こそこそ is a mimetic word describing secretive, furtive, or sneaky behavior.\n\nUSAGE:\nUsually has a negative connotation, implying someone is doing something suspicious or trying to hide something.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- こそこそする: to act sneakily\n- こそこそ⟦{話|はな}す→話す：00467_hanasu⟧: to whisper secretively\n- こそこそ⟦{逃|に}げる→逃げる：01151_nigeru⟧: to sneak away\n- こそこそ⟦{隠|かく}れる→隠れる：02035_kakureru⟧: to hide furtively\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{堂々|どうどう}→堂々：05895_doudou⟧⟦と→と：00512_to⟧: openly, boldly (opposite nuance)\n- ⟦{密|ひそ}かに→密かに：05727_hisokani⟧: secretly (more neutral/literary)",
